# amendment 3 2026-11-15 (buttons-probe.mjs), found on the after-fix WebKit run (39 of 76 style checks failed on "active" only, Chrome 0): two artefacts of driving WebKit with a mouse, traced with the :active chain: (a) after a press released away from the button, Playwright WebKit marks the NEXT hovered element :active with no press, so that button's "not pressed" snapshot already looked pressed; a second mouseup with no button down (fires no click) clears it; (b) a mouse event right after scrollIntoView is hit-tested at the old scroll position, so the press missed the button; the probe now waits 200 ms after scrolling. The pressed-vs-not-pressed comparison, the properties, the candidates and every other check are unchanged.
